            <ArticleTitle>Sequential implantation of dissimilar tandem stents for long dissections complicating percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>155-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute closure remains a significant complication of percutaneous angioplasty, and coronary artery stenting serves as a useful bail-out device. We describe two cases of sequential implantation of dissimilar tandem stents, a Gianturco-Roubin (4 x 20mm) stent and a Palmaz-Schatz (4 x 15mm) stent, for long dissection complicating percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
